<title>GERMANY: D.Babcock wins 170 mln dm of India order.</title>
<headline>D.Babcock wins 170 mln dm of India order.</headline>
<dateline>OBERHAUSEN, Germany 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Babcock AG said on Friday it has signed a letter of intent as part of an international consortium for a 500 million mark ($310.9 million) power plant order awarded by India's SPIC Electric Power Corporation.</p>
<p>The consortium included Babcock unit Babcock Lentjes Kraftwerkstechnik GmbH and Raytheon unit Raytheon Engineers &amp; Constructors.</p>
<p>Babcock said its share of the order was 170 million marks and that the consortium would build a 525 megawatt plant in the Indian state of Tamil Nadu that would begin operating in the year 2000 and could be expanded to 1,050 megawatts.</p>
<p>SPIC Electric is a subsidiary of Southern Petrochemical Industries Corp.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150 ($ = 1.608 German Marks)</p>
